# E++ Programming Language Documentation

Welcome to the official documentation for the **E++** programming language.

## Overview
E++ is a high-performance, structured programming language designed for building modern applications, including scalable social media platforms and backend systems.

## Project Structure
- **`include/`**: Core engine header files (`eplusplus.h`)
- **`src/`**: Main compiler/interpreter execution logic (`main.c`)
- **`lib/`**: Built-in system libraries (e.g., `network.h`)
- **`examples/`**: Code snippets and practical usage examples (`basic_demo.c`)
- **`docs/`**: Official project documentation and manuals

## Getting Started
To compile and test the E++ engine, use a standard C compiler:

```bash
gcc src/main.c -Iinclude -o eplusplus
./eplusplus
